Module T3.2 – AI-Generated Student Feedback Practices

This sample feedback report demonstrates the kind of AI-generated feedback educators can review and personalize. Upload this file into the Module T3.2 simulator to see a demonstration AI response.

SAMPLE AI-GENERATED FEEDBACK REPORT:

Student: [Student Name] | Assignment: Lab Report – Water Cycle | Date: [Date]
Teacher Review Status: PENDING TEACHER REVIEW ⚠️

--- AI-GENERATED FEEDBACK DRAFT ---

Strengths Identified:
• Your diagram of the water cycle clearly labels evaporation, condensation, and precipitation
• The hypothesis was stated in an "If...then...because" format as required
• Data table is organized and includes units of measurement

Areas for Growth:
• The conclusion section does not yet connect your results back to the original hypothesis
• Consider adding specific data points to support your claims (e.g., "The temperature rose by 3°C...")
• The sources section needs at least one scientific journal or database reference

Suggested Next Steps:
1. Revise your conclusion to include: "My hypothesis was [supported/not supported] because..."
2. Add 2-3 specific numbers from your data to your analysis paragraph
3. Visit the school library database to find one peer-reviewed source

--- END AI DRAFT – TEACHER MUST REVIEW BEFORE SHARING WITH STUDENT ---

Teacher Notes: [Add personalized observations here before sending]

